# Database

PostgreSQL with Prisma lives only in `packages/database`. Other packages depend on that client or on repository ports; React code must never import Prisma.

Add a new migration for every schema change. Never edit a migration that may already have been applied.

Use transactions for envelope and signature state transitions. Keep transactions short: no HTTP, no object-storage I/O, no PDF rendering inside a transaction. Perform storage work first or after, with idempotent reconciliation.

Audit tables are append-only. Persist timestamps in UTC. Public IDs are opaque, not serial integers.

```prisma
// ❌ BAD — sequential public id
model Envelope {
  id Int @id @default(autoincrement())
}

// ✅ GOOD — opaque id generated in application code (prefer UUIDv7)
model Envelope {
  id        String   @id
  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @db.Timestamptz
}
```

Do not put business invariants only in the database if the domain must enforce them; keep checks in domain/application code and add constraints where they prevent corruption.
